  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "longitudinal-overview",
      "title": "Poverty levels and change over time",
      "summary": "Annual trends, source-consistent county estimates and correctly identified historical benchmarks",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "longitudinal-overview-period",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The annual chapters use standard ACS one-year estimates. The county directory uses the 2020–2024 ACS five-year release. The historical chapter identifies each source by its actual measurement period, keeping the 1999-income Census benchmark distinct from the two ACS five-year periods.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "longitudinal-comparison-guide",
            "longitudinal-current-c17002",
            "longitudinal-sf3-1999"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "longitudinal-overview-definition",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The population consists of people for whom poverty status was determined. Below twice the poverty threshold includes people below poverty; these cumulative groups overlap. The seven source income-ratio bands are disjoint and remain available in every editable dataset.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "longitudinal-current-c17002"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "longitudinal-overview-uncertainty",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Original 90% component margins of error travel with every ACS source. Derived sum and percentage margins are blank. Changes shown here are descriptive estimates; they do not establish statistical significance or causes.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "longitudinal-comparison-guide"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "longitudinal-history",
      "title": "Ohio historical sources with their actual periods",
      "summary": "1999 income; 2006–2010 and 2020–2024 ACS five-year estimates",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "longitudinal-history-source",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The retained 2026 report transcription labels its baseline 2010. Its Ohio population 11,046,987 and below-twice-poverty count 2,919,858 match the 2000 Census SF3 table measuring 1999 income. The working table preserves that benchmark under its actual period and includes the separately received 2006–2010 ACS source.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "longitudinal-original-report",
            "longitudinal-sf3-1999",
            "longitudinal-acs-2010"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "longitudinal-history-change",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Across the nonoverlapping ACS periods 2006–2010 and 2020–2024, Ohio’s below-twice-poverty estimate changes from 3,561,514 people (31.8%) to 3,372,969 (29.3%). That is 188,545 fewer people and a 2.5 percentage-point decrease. The relative rate change is −7.9%; percentage points and relative percent change describe different calculations.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "longitudinal-acs-2010",
            "longitudinal-current-c17002",
            "longitudinal-comparison-guide"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "longitudinal-annual-ohio",
      "title": "Ohio annual poverty trend",
      "summary": "Standard ACS one-year estimates, 2018–2024",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "longitudinal-annual-ohio-gap",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The 2020 standard one-year release was not produced. Its blank row represents a source gap, not zero poverty. Experimental 2020 estimates are excluded from this comparison. Bars show only available standard years; the table preserves the missing year explicitly.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "longitudinal-standard-gap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "longitudinal-annual-ohio-change",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "From 2019 to 2024, the Ohio poverty-determined population estimate rises by 221,392, while the below-poverty estimate falls by 16,879, from 1,484,862 to 1,467,983. The below-poverty count change is −1.1%. These annual source counts agree with the original Table 9 transcription.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "longitudinal-annual-ohio-2019",
            "longitudinal-annual-ohio-2024",
            "longitudinal-original-report"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "longitudinal-annual-us",
      "title": "United States annual poverty trend",
      "summary": "Standard ACS one-year estimates, 2018–2024",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "longitudinal-annual-us-gap",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The 2020 standard one-year release was not produced. Its blank row represents a source gap, not zero poverty. Experimental 2020 estimates are excluded from this comparison. Bars show only available standard years; the table preserves the missing year explicitly.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "longitudinal-standard-gap"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "longitudinal-counties",
      "title": "Income below twice poverty: every Ohio county",
      "summary": "2020–2024 ACS five-year estimates",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "longitudinal-counties-definition",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The directory uses one consistent five-year source for all 88 counties. Ohio’s statewide row is a benchmark from that same source and overlaps every county. Counts and rates use each geography’s poverty-determined population; county values and the state row must not be added together.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "longitudinal-current-c17002"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "longitudinal-counties-concordance",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Seventy-eight geography rows in the retained Table 11 transcription match all three checked current values: population, below-twice-poverty count and percentage. The other transcribed rows contain missing or merged cells. The editable directory uses the complete received source values and retains every original transcription in the concordance.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "longitudinal-current-c17002",
            "longitudinal-original-report"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
